    "done_when": "Produce the reuse map for the resolution-strategy wave on converged-forward-solve, locked by the lead on 2026-10-10. Read the decision and the six new followups in docs/plans/converged-forward-solve.html: f-cfs-book-read-fragments, f-cfs-map-runtime-operands, f-cfs-exterior-on-exact-support, f-cfs-coupling-build-scale, f-cfs-read-ten-thousand and f-cfs-read-compile-route. Done when the report at the assigned path gives, for each followup:\n(1) the production code it changes, as file and line, with the call path a solve takes through it: the support partition and the booker's one-hole-free-polygon contract; every array captured as a program constant in the map and solve programs, with its shape at about 2,000 cells; build_machine's coupling assembly; the topology read's component-label propagation; and the read's five kernel stages;\n(2) existing code that already does or nearly does the job, in nova (nova/, benchmarks/, scripts/prototypes/, especially scripts/prototypes/support/geometry.py and scripts/prototypes/order2/read.py), in imas-ambix (~/Code/imas-ambix) and in reckon, each with file and line, what it covers and what is missing;\n(3) a proposed node scope with exclusive write paths, so that file-disjoint nodes can run in parallel and conflicting ones are sequenced, stating which pairs share a file;\n(4) the measurement each node's done-when should name (cells, cases, job shape, H200 or titan or CPU rung), copied from the followup.\nRead only: change no file outside the report path. Search named subtrees, never a repository root.",
